<title>UK: Sunderland slide after loss to Southampton.</title>
<headline>Sunderland slide after loss to Southampton.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sunderland Plc crashed 37.5p to 490p after a crucial 1-0 defeat by Southampton in a premier league relegation battle on Tuesday night.</p>
<p>Southampton added 8.5p to 99p, reflecting increased optimism that they will retain their place in the lucrative 20-club elite of English soccer.</p>
<p>Sunderland hover just two points above the relegation zone and the three clubs below them all have games in hand. Southampton are now a point ahead of Sunderland.</p>
</text>
